# The strip's `󰐕` (its cell at column 47 with ` alpha.zig 󰅖 ` before
# it — the tree is 30 wide) drops Rust's `Create…` menu (frame x 47)
# on either button; a hover on
# `New ▸` opens its child hung from the row (its first row one below);
# the child paints no highlight until a row is hovered, then a row
# whose label leaves room carries a `⋮` kebab in its last two cells
# (the frame is wide enough for the rows' chords, so every leaf has the
# room); the kebab's menu offers
# Pin / Hide / Copy; a right-click on a child row offers the same, and
# Enter pins it — the pinned row then leads the menu.
write alpha.zig "const alpha = 1;\n"
open alpha.zig
rightclick 47 1
expect screen contains "┌ Create…"
hover 50 3
expect screen contains "Scratch buffer"
expect screen lacks "HTTP request        ⋮"
hover 72 4
expect screen contains "Scratch buffer      ⋮ │"
hover 72 6
expect screen contains "HTTP request        ⋮"
click 93 6
expect screen contains "Pin to top"
expect screen lacks "Rename…"
key esc
click 47 1
expect screen contains "┌ Create…"
hover 50 3
rightclick 72 5
expect screen contains "Pin to top"
key enter
expect screen contains "pinned scratch.from_clipboard"
click 47 1
expect screen contains "From clipboard"
